{
"about":"Shape outlines both phones build (ShapeGeometry.path), and the settings they keep (shapeParams). Shape ids are the design file's (the iPhone's: star-5, seal, speech; Android's star, badge, speech-bubble through Interchange). paths: shape, w, h, radius and params; path is the outline at w x h, or null for a shape not built here (the rectangle and the circle, drawn as primitives, and the curves but the two callouts). A straight-sided shape is its corners in a 0...100 box, each then scaled by w/100 and h/100. A star: 2 x points corners, k = 0, 1, ..., at angle -pi/2 + k x pi/points (y down), the even ones at 50 from (50,50), the odd ones at 50 x inner (star-5 5/0.4, star-4 4/0.24, star-6 6/0.52, star-8 8/0.64, seal 12/0.84, burst-16 16/0.76). A polygon (pentagon 5, hexagon 6, octagon 8): sides corners on that circle from -pi/2 (a corner straight up) for an odd count, -pi/2 + pi/sides (a flat top) for an even one, each next 2 pi/sides on. An arrow from head (a share of its length) and shaft (a share of its breadth): arrow-right (0,50-50s) (100-100h,50-50s) (100-100h,10) (100,50) (100-100h,90) (100-100h,50+50s) (0,50+50s); left, down and up that turned; arrow-double (0,50) (h,15) (h,lo) (100-h,lo) (100-h,15) (100,50) (100-h,85) (100-h,hi) (h,hi) (h,85). chevron (0,0) (100-n,0) (100,50) (100-n,100) (0,100) (n,50); ribbon (0,20) (100,20) (100-n,50) (100,80) (0,80) (n,50); tag (0,50-n) (60,0) (100,0) (100,100) (60,100) (0,50+n), n = notch x 100 (a tag's notch is half its tip's height: 0 a point, 0.5 square). The others their library path's corners. Repeated corners are dropped. Each corner V between P (before) and N (after) is filleted: a = |PV|, b = |NV|, theta the angle PVN, r = min(radius, min(a,b)/2), t = r / tan(theta/2); when t > min(a,b)/2, t = min(a,b)/2 and r = t x tan(theta/2); a corner where the outline runs straight on is not rounded. The arc runs from V + (P-V)/a x t to V + (N-V)/b x t, sweep 1 when (V-P) x (N-V) > 0, else 0. Written M (first) or L to its start, then A r,r 0 0 sweep end; a corner with no rounding is just M or L to V; Z at the end. Numbers to the hundredth, halves away from zero, a whole number with no point. The callouts (speech, thought) ignore the radius: each is the library's path with its tail's tip at (tailX x w, tailY x h). Settings are held to their reach (points 4...24 and sides 3...12 whole, inner 0.2...0.9, head 0.1...0.9 (a double arrow's 0.1...0.5), shaft 0.1...0.9, tailX 0...1, tailY 0...1.4, notch 0...0.5); absent ones take the shape's own. handles: where a shape's diamond sits with its params, as shares of its box (null: none) - a star's first inner corner, the corner where an arrow's shaft meets its head (on the top side, or the left for up and down), a callout's tail tip, a chevron's or ribbon's notch (n, 0.5), a tag's tip's top corner (0, 0.5 - n). dragged: the shapeParams kept after a diamond is dragged to to - a star's inner its distance from the middle / 0.5, an arrow's head and shaft from the corner (shaft = 1 - 2 x its distance in from the side), a tail's tip there, a notch from its place (a tag's 0.5 - y). writes: the shapeParams an element keeps after params are set (null: none), only what its shape takes and differs from its own (by more than 1e-9), each held to its reach.",
